                            <div class="frame__ruler-v">
                                <span>0</span>
                                <span>3</span>
                                <span>6</span>
                                <span>9</span>
                            </div>
                            <div class="frame__page">
                                <span class="frame__page-mark">W</span>
                                <b>No document open</b>
                                <span>Create a document or open one at a path.</span>
                                <span class="frame__page-note">The page renderer is not implemented.</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="frame__status">
                    <span>Ready</span>
                    <span class="spacer"></span>
                    <span>preview</span>
                    <span>engine not connected</span>
                    <span>zoom 100%</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="work">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Current state</span>
                    <h2>What works today</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Three buckets, no rounding up. A green build is not a working product.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cols-3">
                <article class="work-card">
                    <header>
                        <span class="status-dot" data-state="active"></span>
                        <h3>Framework</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--accent">available</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Workspace build and static bundles.</li>
                        <li>CLI surface and JSON-RPC entry points.</li>
                        <li>Capability matrix that claims nothing.</li>
                        <li>Studio shell with sidebar, canvas and inspector.</li>
                        <li>Skills package scaffolding.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="work-card">
                    <header>
                        <span class="status-dot" data-state="done"></span>
                        <h3>Contracts</h3>
                        <span class="chip chip--accent">available</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Document handle API and close lifecycle.</li>
                        <li>Revisions carried on every summary and report.</li>
                        <li>Stable error codes, including the not-implemented one.</li>
                        <li>Per-format import, edit and export classification.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="work-card work-card--quiet">
                    <header>
                        <span class="status-dot" data-state="planned"></span>
                        <h3>Not yet</h3>
                        <span class="chip">not implemented</span>
                    </header>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Authoring engine for paragraphs, tables and links.</li>
                        <li>Template fill with placeholder coverage.</li>
                        <li>DOCX round-trip and loss reporting.</li>
                        <li>Page renderer and zoom controls.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="pillars">
            <article class="pillar">
                <div class="pillar__top">
                    <span class="pillar__index">01</span>
                    <h2>Authoring</h2>
                    <span class="chip">planned</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Sections, paragraphs, tables and links keep stable ids.
                    Revisions are explicit, so one save cannot silently overwrite
                    another edit. The editor that produces them is still being
                    built.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="pillar">
                <div class="pillar__top">
                    <span class="pillar__index">02</span>
                    <h2>Templates</h2>
                    <span class="chip">planned</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Start from a branded template and fill named placeholders.
                    Coverage and overflow are reported per section, and a value is
                    never assumed to fit.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="pillar">
                <div class="pillar__top">
                    <span class="pillar__index">03</span>
                    <h2>Review</h2>
                    <span class="chip">declared</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                    Checks for styles, fonts, images, sections, tables and links
                    are part of the contract. Findings point at a revision and an
                    object id, never at a page number.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <section class="workflow">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Intended loop</span>
                    <h2>Outline, author, inspect, export</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Each step is tagged by what exists: the contract, or a plan.</p>
            </div>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li class="step">
                    <span class="step__index">01</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="step__top">
                            <h3>Outline</h3>
                            <span class="chip">declared</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Sections and paragraph summaries are in the document contract. The studio already reserves a rail for them.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="step">
                    <span class="step__index">02</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="step__top">
                            <h3>Author</h3>
                            <span class="chip">planned</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>Edit paragraphs, tables and links as objects. No authoring command is wired to a document handle yet.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="step">
                    <span class="step__index">03</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="step__top">
                            <h3>Inspect</h3>
                            <span class="chip">declared</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>The six checks are declared in the matrix; the inspection call returns the stable not-implemented code.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="step">
                    <span class="step__index">04</span>
                    <div>
                        <div class="step__top">
                            <h3>Export</h3>
                            <span class="chip">declared</span>
                        </div>
                        <p>docx, dotx, pdf, html and md are declared targets. No writer exists, so no file is produced.</p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="workflow__note">Tags describe the contract, not a working action. No step runs end to end yet.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="formats">
            <div class="section-head">
                <div>
                    <span class="eyebrow">Declared surface</span>
                    <h2>Format matrix</h2>
                </div>
                <p>Every cell comes from the same capability matrix the studio reads at runtime.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Format</th>
                            <th scope="col">Import</th>
                            <th scope="col">Edit</th>
                            <th scope="col">Export</th>
                            <th scope="col">Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr v-for="row in formats" :key="row.name">
                            <td class="mono">.{{ row.name }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.importState }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.editState }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.exportState }}</td>
                            <td><span class="status-dot" data-state="planned"></span> {{ row.status }}</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="formats__note">A suffix is not a support claim. Declared formats stay unsupported until the matrix says otherwise.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="band">
            <div>
                <span class="eyebrow">Status</span>
                <h2>In development · no public release</h2>
                <p>
                    The contracts, capability matrix and studio shell exist.
                    Authoring, template fill, DOCX exchange and the page renderer
                    do not. The roadmap keeps that distinction in every phase.
                </p>
            </div>
            <Link to="RoadmapPage" class="btn btn--ghost">
